 that. In the final the leaders at the turn were the Unified Team’s Volkov and " [:a {:href "/athletes/50814"} "Vasily Ivanov"] ", with Diebel third, but the Russians faded on the second lap and Diebel came on for a shocking gold medal, with Rózsa hanging on for the silver, the bronze going to Australia’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/63483"} "Philip Rogers"] ". Diebel’s time was only the 13th-best performance ever and had been bettered four times by Rózsa, but Diebel had the gold."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "B Final"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "606"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/51318"} "Nelson Diebel"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "1:01.80 (2 h6)"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "1:01.50 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "335"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/48228"} "Norbert Rózsa"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/HUN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/HUN.png"}] "HUN"]] [:td {} "1:02.25 (3 h8)"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "1:01.68 (2)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {:class "bib"} "36"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/45278"} "Phil Rogers"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/AUS"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/AUS.png"}] "AUS"]] [:td {} "1:02.10 (2 h8)"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "1:01.76 (3)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Bronze"} "Bronze"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style "